{#-
  The systemd slice every Fabro sandbox container on this host joins, because the
  Docker daemon names it as its default `cgroup-parent`.

  EVERY LIMIT COMES FROM A ROLE VARIABLE AND NONE IS SPELLED HERE. The "Sandbox
  resource envelope" paragraph of the `## Fabro factory host provisioning` section
  of SPECIFICATION/non-functional-requirements.md requires the slice's limits to be
  read from role variables; a number inline here would be an envelope no host could
  resize from its host_vars, which is the whole purpose of an interim control.

  THE TEMPLATE STAYS A SUBSTITUTION TEMPLATE. No filter, no conditional, no loop —
  tests/consumer/test_docker_sandbox_slice_scenario.py renders it by substituting
  `{{ name }}` and nothing else (neither Ansible nor Jinja is importable in that
  suite), and it fails deliberately if this template leaves that vocabulary rather
  than letting the renderer quietly disagree with Jinja about what the host gets.
-#}
# {{ ansible_managed }}
[Unit]
Description=Aggregate resource envelope for this host's Fabro sandbox containers
Documentation=https://github.com/thewoolleyman/livespec-dev-tooling/tree/master/ansible/roles/docker_sandbox_slice
Before=slices.target

[Slice]
MemoryHigh={{ docker_sandbox_slice_memory_high }}
MemoryMax={{ docker_sandbox_slice_memory_max }}
CPUQuota={{ docker_sandbox_slice_cpu_quota }}
